description:
In rust/lichen-oscore/src/edhoc.rs, the rfc9529_signature_trace_vectors test previously included a full EdhocInitiator::process_message_2_with_credential verification:
```rust
let mut verifier = EdhocInitiator::new_with_rng(...)
verifier.create_message_1()...
let verified_message_3 = verifier.process_message_2_with_credential(
    &message_2,
    PeerCredential::new(&responder_public_key, &id_cred_r, &credential_r),
);
assert!(verified_message_3.is_ok(), ...);
```
This was removed alongside the test vector updates. While process_message_2_with_credential is still called in test_full_smoke_handshake (line ~2223), the RFC 9529 trace vectors no longer verify that the full initiator flow produces the expected message_3 output from the known RFC test vectors. This is a regression in test coverage for cross-implementation validation.
